[PROJECT_OVERVIEW]
name: OpenGL Engine & Editor
description: C++20 3D graphics engine with real-time scene editor
tech_stack:
  - C++20 (no extensions)
  - OpenGL 4.5+ rendering
  - ImGui editor UI
  - CMake build system
  - EnTT ECS framework
  - Assimp model importing
  - Boost 1.84.0 utilities

[PROJECT_PURPOSE]
goal: Build production-quality 3D engine with WYSIWYG editor
key_features:
  - Data-driven scene management (world_desc → prefabs → entities)
  - Multi-world ECS (up to 8 independent worlds)
  - Real-time render pipeline with extractors and passes
  - Async asset loading with resource cache
  - In-editor prefab and shader editing
  - Hot-reload descriptor system

[ARCHITECTURE_TIERS]
Layer 1: Core Services
  - ECS engine, window management, resource system
  - Configuration system, application lifecycle
  - Memory allocators, logging

Layer 2: Engine Systems
  - Scene management, camera, lighting
  - Render pipeline (extractors → passes)
  - Input handling, physics integration hooks
  - Animation and skinning systems

Layer 3: Editor Application
  - ImGui-based scene editor
  - Inspector, hierarchy, asset browser
  - Gizmo-based object transformation
  - Prefab editor with live preview

[CURRENT_STATUS]
active_epics: 48 total
completed: ~28 (core infra, render migration, editor basics)
in_progress: EPIC-25 (Prefab Editor), EPIC-33 (Skinning & Animation)
upcoming: Optimization, shader/texture descriptors, workspace system

[CRITICAL_PATHS]
Prefab System:
  EPIC-12 ✅ → EPIC-13 ✅ → EPIC-14 ✅ → EPIC-25 🔄

Render Pipeline:
  EPIC-16-21 ✅ → EPIC-45 (optimization) → EPIC-48 (GPU batching)

Infrastructure:
  EPIC-23,37-39,43 ✅ → EPIC-44,46-47

[KEY_CONSTRAINTS]
- C++20 only, no compiler extensions
- Tabs (size 4) for all indentation
- No global state in performance-critical code
- All logging via engine_log.h, never std::cout
- Frame allocator for temp data, never across frames
